{"annotator_prompt": [{"kind": "delete", "field": "holding"}],
 "policy_prompt_for_memory": [{"kind": "delete", "field": "holding"}],
 "policy_prompt_for_subgoal": [
  {"modify_from": "In every rule below, `holding` means the value written for this decision step (the state of the fingers in the scene now), not the value carried in; the carried-in value is still `none` at the step right after a grasp. In-hand is read from the gripper alone:", "modify_to": "In every rule below, what is in hand is read from the gripper in the scene at this decision step alone, never from memory:"},
  {"modify_from": "- If `method` is `pick` and `holding` is `none`: choose D (pick up the cube). - If `method` is `pick` and `holding` is `cube`: choose E (place the cube onto the target). - If `method` is `hook` and `holding` is `none`: choose A (pick up the peg). - If `method` is `hook` and `holding` is `peg`: choose B (hook the cube to the target with the peg).", "modify_to": "- If `method` is `pick` and nothing is in hand: choose D (pick up the cube). - If `method` is `pick` and the cube is in hand: choose E (place the cube onto the target). - If `method` is `hook` and nothing is in hand: choose A (pick up the peg). - If `method` is `hook` and the peg is in hand: choose B (hook the cube to the target with the peg)."}
 ],
 "refused": "Nothing refused. The report's deletion of `holding` is committed on both sides: the field was always one step stale when read and the scene at every decision step recovers the same fact, so it fails NECESSITY. This does not undo round 1, whose substance (judging in-hand from gripper height and finger opening in the current scene, not from object coordinates or held marks) stays in the subgoal instruction; only the detour through a memory field is removed. The memory now holds `method` alone, which is the one fact only the first decision step shows."}
